#: ../../../builtins-easy.rst:130
msgid ""
"``list`` on a string iterates its characters, producing a one-character "
"string per element."
msgstr ""
"``list`` sobre una cadena itera sus caracteres, produciendo una cadena de un"
" solo carácter por elemento."

#: ../../../builtins-easy.rst:147 ../../../builtins-easy.rst:171
#: ../../../builtins-easy.rst:246 ../../../builtins-easy.rst:419
msgid "``1``"
msgstr "``1``"

#: ../../../builtins-easy.rst:149 ../../../builtins-easy.rst:174
msgid "``9``"
msgstr "``9``"

#: ../../../builtins-easy.rst:150
msgid "``16``"
msgstr "``16``"

#: ../../../builtins-easy.rst:155
msgid "``max`` returns the largest item of the iterable, which is ``9``."
msgstr "``max`` devuelve el elemento mayor del iterable, que es ``9``."

#: ../../../builtins-easy.rst:172 ../../../builtins-easy.rst:245
msgid "``2``"
msgstr "``2``"

#: ../../../builtins-easy.rst:179
msgid "``min`` returns the smallest item of the iterable, which is ``1``."
msgstr "``min`` devuelve el elemento menor del iterable, que es ``1``."

#: ../../../builtins-easy.rst:196
msgid "``[0, 1, 2]``"
msgstr "``[0, 1, 2]``"

#: ../../../builtins-easy.rst:197
msgid "``[0, 1, 2, 3]``"
msgstr "``[0, 1, 2, 3]``"

#: ../../../builtins-easy.rst:198
msgid "``[3]``"
msgstr "``[3]``"

#: ../../../builtins-easy.rst:203
msgid ""
"``range(3)`` yields ``0, 1, 2`` — it starts at ``0`` and stops *before* the "
"given stop value."
msgstr ""
"``range(3)`` produce ``0, 1, 2`` — empieza en ``0`` y se detiene *antes* del"
" valor de parada indicado."

#: ../../../builtins-easy.rst:221
msgid "``\"100\"``"
msgstr "``\"100\"``"

#: ../../../builtins-easy.rst:222
msgid "``1.0``"
msgstr "``1.0``"

#: ../../../builtins-easy.rst:223
msgid "``100``"
msgstr "``100``"

#: ../../../builtins-easy.rst:228
msgid "``int`` parses a decimal string into an integer, giving ``100``."
msgstr ""
"``int`` analiza una cadena decimal y la convierte en un entero, dando "
"``100``."

#: ../../../builtins-easy.rst:252
msgid "``len`` of a ``dict`` counts its keys; there are 2."
msgstr "``len`` de un ``dict`` cuenta sus claves; hay 2."

#: ../../../builtins-easy.rst:268
msgid "``[('x', 0), ('y', 1)]``"
msgstr "``[('x', 0), ('y', 1)]``"

#: ../../../builtins-easy.rst:269
msgid "``[(1, 'x'), (2, 'y')]``"
msgstr "``[(1, 'x'), (2, 'y')]``"

#: ../../../builtins-easy.rst:270
msgid "``[(0, 'x'), (1, 'y')]``"
msgstr "``[(0, 'x'), (1, 'y')]``"

#: ../../../builtins-easy.rst:271
msgid "``['x', 'y']``"
msgstr "``['x', 'y']``"

#: ../../../builtins-easy.rst:276
msgid ""
"``enumerate`` pairs each item with a counter starting at ``0``, yielding "
"``(index, value)`` tuples."
msgstr ""
"``enumerate`` empareja cada elemento con un contador que empieza en ``0``, "
"produciendo tuplas ``(index, value)``."

#: ../../../builtins-easy.rst:301
msgid "The number ``0`` is falsy, so ``bool(0)`` is ``False``."
msgstr "El número ``0`` es falso, así que ``bool(0)`` es ``False``."

#: ../../../builtins-easy.rst:317
msgid "``['a', 'b', 'c', 'd']``"
msgstr "``['a', 'b', 'c', 'd']``"

#: ../../../builtins-easy.rst:318
msgid "``'abcd'``"
msgstr "``'abcd'``"

#: ../../../builtins-easy.rst:319
msgid "``['d', 'c', 'b', 'a']``"
msgstr "``['d', 'c', 'b', 'a']``"

#: ../../../builtins-easy.rst:320
msgid "``['dbca']``"
msgstr "``['dbca']``"

#: ../../../builtins-easy.rst:325
msgid ""
"``sorted`` always returns a *list*, even when given a string: it iterates "
"the characters and sorts them."
msgstr ""
"``sorted`` siempre devuelve una *lista*, incluso cuando se le pasa una "
"cadena: itera los caracteres y los ordena."

#: ../../../builtins-easy.rst:342
msgid "``[1, 2]``"
msgstr "``[1, 2]``"

#: ../../../builtins-easy.rst:343 ../../../builtins-easy.rst:369
msgid "``(1, 2)``"
msgstr "``(1, 2)``"

#: ../../../builtins-easy.rst:344 ../../../builtins-easy.rst:370
#, python-brace-format
msgid "``{1, 2}``"
msgstr "``{1, 2}``"

#: ../../../builtins-easy.rst:345
msgid "``(1, 2,)``"
msgstr "``(1, 2,)``"

#: ../../../builtins-easy.rst:350
msgid ""
"``tuple`` builds an immutable sequence from the iterable, printed as ``(1, "
"2)``."
msgstr ""
"``tuple`` construye una secuencia inmutable a partir del iterable, que se "
"imprime como ``(1, 2)``."

#: ../../../builtins-easy.rst:367
msgid "``[1, 1, 2, 2]``"
msgstr "``[1, 1, 2, 2]``"

#: ../../../builtins-easy.rst:368
#, python-brace-format
msgid "``{1, 1, 2, 2}``"
msgstr "``{1, 1, 2, 2}``"

#: ../../../builtins-easy.rst:375
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"A ``set`` holds only unique elements, so the duplicates collapse to ``{1, "
"2}``."
msgstr ""
"Un ``set`` solo contiene elementos únicos, así que los duplicados se reducen"
" a ``{1, 2}``."

#: ../../../builtins-easy.rst:393
msgid "``\"3.5\"``"
msgstr "``\"3.5\"``"

#: ../../../builtins-easy.rst:394
msgid "``3.5``"
msgstr "``3.5``"

#: ../../../builtins-easy.rst:395
msgid "``ValueError``"
msgstr "``ValueError``"

#: ../../../builtins-easy.rst:400
msgid ""
"``float`` parses a numeric string, including a decimal point, into a "
"floating-point number."
msgstr ""
"``float`` analiza una cadena numérica, incluido un punto decimal, y la "
"convierte en un número de coma flotante."

#: ../../../builtins-easy.rst:425
msgid ""
"``any`` is ``True`` if at least one element is truthy; here one ``True`` is "
"enough."
msgstr ""
"``any`` es ``True`` si al menos un elemento tiene valor de verdad verdadero;"
" aquí basta con un ``True``."

#: ../../../builtins-easy.rst:450
msgid ""
"``all`` is ``True`` only if *every* element is truthy; the single ``False`` "
"makes it ``False``."
msgstr ""
"``all`` es ``True`` solo si *todos* los elementos tienen valor de verdad "
"verdadero; el único ``False`` lo hace ``False``."

#: ../../../builtins-easy.rst:475
msgid ""
"``sum`` of an empty iterable returns its start value, which defaults to "
"``0``."
msgstr ""
"``sum`` de un iterable vacío devuelve su valor inicial, que por defecto es "
"``0``."

#: ../../../builtins-easy.rst:492
msgid "``(2, 3)``"
msgstr "``(2, 3)``"

#: ../../../builtins-easy.rst:493
msgid "``3.4``"
msgstr "``3.4``"

#: ../../../builtins-easy.rst:494
msgid "``(3, 2)``"
msgstr "``(3, 2)``"

#: ../../../builtins-easy.rst:495
msgid "``(3.4, 0)``"
msgstr "``(3.4, 0)``"

#: ../../../builtins-easy.rst:500
msgid ""
"``divmod(a, b)`` returns ``(a // b, a % b)`` — the quotient ``3`` and the "
"remainder ``2``."
msgstr ""
"``divmod(a, b)`` devuelve ``(a // b, a % b)`` — el cociente ``3`` y el resto"
" ``2``."
